#X obj 668 8 chaos.jong;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 391 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A non-interpolating chaotic generator based on the Peter
de Jong attractor \, a two-dimensional discrete dynamical system. On
each bang the generator advances the map by one step and outputs the
new x and y coordinates.;
#X text 240 153 The attractor is defined by the difference equations:;
#X text 240 178 x[n+1] = sin(a * y[n]) - cos(b * x[n]);
#X text 240 203 y[n+1] = sin(c * x[n]) - cos(d * y[n]);
#X text 240 228 The shape of the trajectory depends strongly on the
parameters a \, b \, c and d. The default values (a = 1.4 \, b = -2.3
\, c = 2.4 \, d = -2.1) produce a rich \, structured chaotic pattern.
Other parameter sets give very different shapes — some are dense clouds
\, others are ring-like or spiral structures.;
#X text 240 329 The output values are in the range of approximately
-2 to 2 for both x and y. Because interpolation is not used \, the
values jump between discrete points when driven by a slow metro — this
makes the object useful as a source of stepped chaotic control signals
for filters \, pan positions or pitches.;
#X obj 240 433 ui.link @background_color 0.90196 0.90196 0.90196
@title wiki: Peter de Jong Attractors @url
http://paulbourke.net/fractals/peterdejong/;
